well we do want to say here it is we're  officially one week away from the 2020  general election  so far more than 258 000 people in clark  county  have turned out for early voting a news  now reporter kate houston spoke to the  election department  about some of the top questions they're  getting from voters  with only a few days left of early  voting some community members came out  to silver mesa recreation center to cast  their ballot  dan kulin with the election department  says while the polls have been busy  so have the phone lines the county's 455  vote hotline is receiving more than 2  thousand calls a day  voters can call basically with any  question  it's a good starting point for folks who  are looking for information  some top questions from voters are if  they're allowed to vote in person after  receiving a mail ballot and where they  should go  years ago we had assigned precincts we  had to go to a very specific polling  place that was near our house  but we've changed that and so now any  voter in clark county can vote at any  polling place on election day just like  in early voting  registration is another question they  get so far  more than 1.2 million nevadans are  registered to vote in this election  we do have same-day registration in  nevada  and so if folks aren't registered to  vote they still can register at their  polling place  when it comes to mailing your ballot  kulin says it has to be postmarked on  or before november 3rd know that once  turned in  the decisions on your ballot cannot be  changed if they're going to be voting in  person  we would strongly suggest that they mark  their sample ballot  with their selections and then bring it  with them so that they can  you know use their sample ballot to make  sure they're making the choices they  want to make  early voting will last through october  30th kate houston 8 news now  in addition to the 400 or rather 455  vote hotline you can also go to the  election department's website  there is information on voting locations  registration and much more  that can be found at clarkcountynv.gov  vote denise
 

